{"sections":[],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P8CoveringE20minimumDominatingSetSay6VertexQzGyF","title":"minimumDominatingSet()","role":"symbol","modules":[{"relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"],"name":"Covering"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"ExactCovering.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Covering\/ExactCovering.swift#L1846"},"roleHeading":"Instance Method","symbolKind":"method","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"minimumDominatingSet","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"extendedModule":"GraphProtocols"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/minimumDominatingSet()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A minimum dominating set (exact): every vertex is in it or adjacent to one in it, and of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the smallest such sets it is the lexicographically least by vertex index (the rule of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maximumIndependentSet()"},{"type":"text","text":"), in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order; [] for the empty graph. Self-loops and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"parallel edges do not matter; isolated vertices are in it."}],"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/minimumdominatingset()"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"minimumDominatingSet"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each connected component is solved alone; a vertex adjacent to all the others of its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"component answers alone. Otherwise branch and reduce: after every choice, an undominated"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex with one possible dominator gets it, and a vertex whose undominated closed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"neighbourhood lies in another’s is ruled out (for the lexicographic pass only in favour of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a lesser vertex, which keeps the least set; this leaf rule settles paths and many trees"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"outright). The search branches on the most-coverage dominator of an undominated vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with the fewest left and prunes on the budget, on the largest coverages, and on a greedy"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"2-packing (vertices with no dominator in common, each needing its own; on trees the largest"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"2-packing is γ, Meir and Moon 1975). γ comes from a greedy descent and decisions one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"smaller; the least set of γ vertices is then decided vertex by vertex in index order"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"against a witness, each decision searching only the part of the problem the vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"touches. Sparse components keep O(n + m) words of state; dense ones (mean degree d with d²"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"above c ⌈c \/ 64⌉) use bitset closed neighbourhoods, under 2m words. Exponential in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"component size in the worst case."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering","doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"references":{"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"abstract":[],"title":"Graph","url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"extension","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P","text":"Graph","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols":{"abstract":[],"title":"GraphProtocols","url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols","role":"collection"},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols/Graph/minimumDominatingSet()":{"kind":"symbol","title":"minimumDominatingSet()","url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/minimumdominatingset()","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/minimumDominatingSet()","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"minimumDominatingSet"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A minimum dominating set (exact): every vertex is in it or adjacent to one in it, and of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the smallest such sets it is the lexicographically least by vertex index (the rule of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"maximumIndependentSet()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), in "},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" order; [] for the empty graph. Self-loops and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"parallel edges do not matter; isolated vertices are in it."}]},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering":{"abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering","title":"Covering","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/covering","type":"topic","role":"collection"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/Graph/Vertex":{"abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","title":"Vertex","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/graph\/vertex","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"associatedtype","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"identifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hashable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]}}}